From 01ccb527fe2f000acde142daba2ada1da0919028 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:37:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Opening a film grows the tapped poster into the header poster
 (rule 1725)

Owner-approved b66-09-open-film, built for build 38. The OPEN only: the
tapped poster flies 450ms on cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1) to the film page's
header poster, the page fades in (220ms), the backdrop fades in (450ms) and
the blocks rise 24px (380ms from 70ms). Transforms and opacity only; the
flying layer is the poster already on screen, handed off to the header once
its poster has loaded, so nothing flashes and a slow page never jumps.

The close is unchanged (rule 1141): web drags the sheet down, iPhone swipes
the full-screen cover down at full width; nothing shrinks, and
navigationTransition(.zoom) stays off. Reduce Motion: a ~200ms crossfade.
Haptic: only the existing light tick.

Built once in the shared path: web in PortalModal's film sheet
(lib/poster-open.ts, a capture-phase tap watch finds the poster), iPhone in
PageStack.openFilm -> FilmCoverPage (Design/PosterFlight.swift, posters
marked by filmZoomSource). No poster under the tap (deep link, push, text
link, restored sheet): today's slide up. Films drilled inside a film page
keep their own change. iPhone not compiled here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013WRDCFXH8nihP92apJAVW7
